<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Market quiet, basis steady.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Market quiet, basis steady.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soymeal dealers reported light to moderate cash sales Wednesday, primarily for prompt shipment.</p>
<p>Buyers continued to resist buying July-delivered soymeal because of the $5- to $7-per-ton basis premium for that position. Because of tight soybean supplies most processors were not pricing soymeal for August delivery.</p>
<p>Tight supplies of old-crop soybeans and high prices for what was available had some dealers expecting Thursday's NOPA weekly crush report to show a slight decline in the crush from the previous week's 25.378 million bushels.  </p>
